# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets -- the only truly non-negotiable entry in this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
*.key
secrets.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived artefacts that can be rebuilt from raw
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The DuckDB file is a build output, not a source. It is rebuilt from scratch on
# every transform run, it is large, and it changes entirely each time -- which
# would make git history useless. Raw Parquet and curated CSV/Parquet ARE
# committed, because those are what Power BI and the website read over HTTPS.
data/warehouse.duckdb
data/warehouse.duckdb.wal

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Power BI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .pbix is a binary zip: git cannot diff it and every save rewrites the whole
# file, so committing it bloats the repo fast. Commit the M and DAX source
# instead -- those are the reviewable artefacts -- plus screenshots.
# EXCEPTION: many reviewers want to open the actual report. If you commit one,
# commit a single release copy (e.g. powerbi/GridForecastAccuracy.pbix) rather
# than every working save, and use Git LFS if it exceeds ~50 MB.
*.pbix.bak
*.pbip.bak
TempState/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Large curated CSV twins (fact_fuel_mix.csv ~52 MB, fact_load_hour.csv ~26 MB).
# Committing them hourly would grow the repo by ~2 GB/day: git cannot delta-
# compress whole-file rewrites of this size. Parquet is what Power BI consumes
# and stays tracked; the small dim_*.csv files stay for quick inspection.
data/curated/fact_*.csv
data/curated/agg_*.csv
.claude/
